# TAGTOP — Environment Configuration Example
# Copy this file to .env for local frontend development.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Frontend / Vite (public, safe to bundle) ──────────────────────────────────
# Used by src/ code to connect the browser to Supabase with the anon key.
# Found in: Supabase Dashboard → Project Settings → API
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-id.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-supabase-public-anon-key

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# !! SECURITY WARNING — SERVICE ROLE KEY !!
#
# NEVER put SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY here or in any VITE_-prefixed variable.
# The service role key bypasses ALL Row Level Security policies.
# It must only be used in trusted server-side code and test harnesses.
#
# For integration tests, copy scripts/.env.test.example → scripts/.env.test
# and add your credentials there. That file is gitignored (.env*).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
